cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the essay it
  implements.
title: "lat — Language as a Tool"
abstract: >-
  A local, read-only Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that serves a curated
  catalogue of natural-language and poetic "thinking patterns", classified by a
  closed set of cognitive axes, for reframing a problem through a contrasting
  language or form.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-23"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Schlifka
    given-names: Dana
repository-code: "https://github.com/nyadyme/lat"
url: "https://github.com/nyadyme/lat"
keywords:
  - MCP
  - Model Context Protocol
  - linguistic relativity
  - reframing
  - thinking tools
  - prior art

# The essay this software implements — canonical, timestamped deposits.
references:
